    "id": 3530358,
    "postDate": "2026-09-30T03:26:42.763Z",
    "rawMarkdown": "The best way to maintain rank on private LB compared to public LB is to \"trust your CV\". Set up a local CV scheme which mimics the relationship between Kaggle test and Kaggle train. (i.e. if Kaggle test has different studies than train, them make your kfold validation have different studies than kfold train).\n\nThe next technique is more advanced. If there are differences in your LB score versus your CV score, you need to do detective work to understand what is different between test and train. And you then extrapolate this conclusion to what may be different between private and public test. Then you adjust/adapt your local validation and model training to handle/accomdate this.",
    "content": "<p>The best way to maintain rank on private LB compared to public LB is to \"trust your CV\". Set up a local CV scheme which mimics the relationship between Kaggle test and Kaggle train. (i.e. if Kaggle test has different studies than train, them make your kfold validation have different studies than kfold train).</p>\n<p>The next technique is more advanced. If there are differences in your LB score versus your CV score, you need to do detective work to understand what is different between test and train. And you then extrapolate this conclusion to what may be different between private and public test. Then you adjust/adapt your local validation and model training to handle/accomdate this.</p>",
