    "postDate": "2026-09-30T02:20:08.163Z",
    "rawMarkdown": "I usually improve the code and then test on my local data to see whether it runs, then submit to Kaggle to check whether the score improves. If it improves, I keep improving the code on top of that new version. My experience from two competitions tells me that local test scores can't reflect the public leaderboard score, but the private leaderboard has a big gap from the public leaderboard score.",
    "content": "<p>I usually improve the code and then test on my local data to see whether it runs, then submit to Kaggle to check whether the score improves. If it improves, I keep improving the code on top of that new version. My experience from two competitions tells me that local test scores can't reflect the public leaderboard score, but the private leaderboard has a big gap from the public leaderboard score.</p>",
